            leo("Hold on. «sie» is she, and «Sie» is the polite you?"),
            maya("They sound the same, so listen to the verb. «sie kommt», she comes. «Sie kommen», you come. On paper, the polite one always has a capital S. Now the friendly part. Frau Weber is pleased to meet her."),
            jonas("Freut mich! Willkommen. [repeat]", "Pleased to meet you! Welcome."),
            leo("When do I say «Freut mich»? When I leave?"),
            maya("No, and that's a classic mistake. «Freut mich» is pleased to meet you, at the start of a first meeting. «Willkommen» is welcome. Now Sanya didn't catch the teacher's name. So she says thank you, and then two very useful words."),
            jonas("Danke. Wie bitte, wie heißen Sie? [repeat]", "Thank you. Sorry, what is your name?"),
            leo("[chuckle] «Wie bitte». My new best friend."),
            maya("It might be the most useful phrase in the whole exam. It means sorry, say that again. It's polite everywhere, and saying nothing helps no one. Then Frau Weber spells her name with the German letter names."),
            jonas("Weber. We, E, Be, E, Er. [repeat]", "Weber. W, E, B, E, R."),
            leo("The W sounds like a v there too. And the E is eh, not ee."),
