            jonas("Sie hat einen Bruder. Haben Sie einen Bruder? [repeat]", "She has a brother. Do you have a brother? (polite)"),
            leo("And it? Like, it has?"),
            maya("That's «es», and it's for das words. «Das Kind» is a das word, so a child is «es», even a little boy. Now try swapping names for these little words. Usaid becomes «er», Sanya becomes «sie», and you plus Usaid become «wir», we."),
            jonas("Usaid hat Zeit. Er hat Zeit. [repeat]", "Usaid has time. He has time."),
            leo("Got it. Now the my and your words."),
            maya("Those are called «Possessivartikel», words that say whose something is. Here's the picture: the word belongs to the thing, not to the owner. It dresses to match the noun. A der or das noun gets plain «mein». A die noun, or a plural, gets «meine»."),
            jonas("Mein Vater, mein Kind. Meine Mutter, meine Eltern. [repeat]", "My father, my child. My mother, my parents."),
