    private val de5Practice = Podcast(
        "de5-practice",
        listOf(
            maya("Welcome back. Today is practice: reading flat adverts, and writing about your new flat. Both are real exam tasks. In the reading part you get a situation and two adverts, and you pick the one that fits. In the writing part, you might tell a friend about your new home."),
            leo("Reading adverts. What's the trick?"),
            maya("Read the situation first, and pick out the two or three conditions. Here's ours: you want a flat for at most six hundred euros, near the station. Jonas reads the question the way the exam writes it."),
            jonas("Sie suchen eine Wohnung für maximal sechshundert Euro in der Nähe vom Bahnhof. Welche Anzeige passt?", "You are looking for a flat for at most six hundred euros near the station. Which advert fits?"),
            leo("«Anzeige» is the advert, I guess. And «passt»?"),
            maya("«passt» means fits, or suits. So: which «Anzeige» fits? Now advert A. Listen for the price and the station."),
            jonas("Zwei-Zimmer-Wohnung, hell und ruhig, fünfhundertachtzig Euro plus Nebenkosten, fünf Minuten zum Bahnhof.", "Two-room flat, bright and quiet, five hundred and eighty euros plus bills, five minutes to the station."),
            leo("Under six hundred, and close to the station. Sounds good."),
            maya("It ticks both boxes. Now advert B."),
            jonas("Drei-Zimmer-Wohnung im Zentrum, mit Balkon, neunhundertfünfzig Euro plus Nebenkosten.", "Three-room flat in the centre, with a balcony, nine hundred and fifty euros plus bills."),
            leo("[laugh] Nine hundred and fifty. That one's out."),
            maya("Right, so A fits. But watch for the decoy. In the exam, the wrong advert usually fits most of the conditions and fails just one. So check every condition, not two out of three. And adverts hide small print. Advert A also says this."),
            jonas("Keine Haustiere. [repeat]", "No pets."),
            leo("«Haustiere» are pets? So no cat."),
            maya("No cat. «keine» is a no. Advert B is the opposite, and it gives a date when the flat is free."),
            jonas("Haustiere willkommen. Ab dem ersten November.", "Pets welcome. From the first of November."),
            leo("So B loves cats but costs a fortune. Okay, now the writing?"),
            maya("The writing task: tell a friend about your new flat. Four points: where it is, how many rooms, what you like, and an invitation. Usaid writes to Sanya. He opens with «Liebe Sanya», dear Sanya, then says where, with «in» plus the dative."),
            jonas("Ich habe eine neue Wohnung! Sie ist im Zentrum, in der Gartenstraße. [repeat]", "I have a new flat! It's in the centre, in Gartenstraße."),
            leo("«im Zentrum», because it's «das Zentrum», and «in dem» glues into «im»?"),
            maya("Exactly. A letter that spells out «in dem» reads like a translation. Second point: the rooms, with «hat»."),
            jonas("Die Wohnung hat drei Zimmer, eine Küche und ein Bad. [repeat]", "The flat has three rooms, a kitchen and a bathroom."),
            leo("Third, what I like. Can I just say it's nice?"),
            maya("Use an adjective after «ist»: «groß», «hell», «ruhig», «schön». And «es gibt» adds a bonus."),
            jonas("Das Wohnzimmer ist groß und hell. Es gibt auch einen kleinen Balkon. [repeat]", "The living room is big and bright. There is also a small balcony."),
            leo("And the invitation?"),
            maya("A question. Then close the way you opened: «Liebe Sanya» goes with «Viele Grüße»."),
            jonas("Kommst du am Samstag? Viele Grüße, Usaid. [repeat]", "Are you coming on Saturday? Best wishes, Usaid."),
            leo("Short and sweet. Is that really enough?"),
            maya("About thirty words, with all four points. The one people forget is where the flat is. Now speaking. In the speaking part you get a topic and a word card. The topic is «Wohnen», living, and the card says «Zimmer». You turn the word into a question."),
            jonas("Wie viele Zimmer hat deine Wohnung? [repeat]", "How many rooms does your flat have?"),
            leo("And my partner answers in a full sentence?"),
            maya("Yes, a full sentence. The rooms, plus a balcony if there is one. It's «der Balkon», so «einen Balkon»."),
            jonas("Meine Wohnung hat zwei Zimmer und einen Balkon. [repeat]", "My flat has two rooms and a balcony."),
            leo("And if I want to say where I live?"),
