            jonas("Achtung am Gleis drei: Der ICE nach München hat heute zwanzig Minuten Verspätung.", "Attention on platform 3: the ICE to Munich is twenty minutes late today."),
            leo("So if the board says it leaves at ten thirty-two, I add twenty?"),
            maya("Yes. The board keeps the planned time, and «Verspätung», the delay, is added to it. Ten thirty-two plus twenty is ten fifty-two. And if the statement says the train is «pünktlich», on time, you answer «Falsch»."),
            jonas("Der Zug hat Verspätung. [repeat]", "The train is late."),
            leo("What's the second announcement?"),
            maya("A «Regionalzug», a regional train, to Bonn. Listen for the little word «nicht». When an announcement corrects itself, the number before «nicht» is the real one."),
            jonas("Der Regionalzug nach Bonn fährt heute von Gleis fünf, nicht von Gleis zwei. [repeat]", "The regional train to Bonn leaves from platform 5 today, not platform 2."),
            leo("Five, not two. Got it. And the last one?"),
            maya("The one just before the doors close. «Liebe Fahrgäste» is dear passengers, «schließen» is to close, and «gleich» means in a moment."),
            jonas("Bitte einsteigen und die Türen schließen. Der Zug fährt gleich ab. [repeat]", "Please board and close the doors. The train is about to depart."),
            leo("So what should I remember for the Goethe exam?"),
            maya("Three things. In «Hören» part two you hear five announcements, once only, so read the statement first and listen for one detail. Catch the platform, the time, «Verspätung» and the word «nicht». And in «Sprechen», «Muss ich umsteigen?» is a perfect question to ask."),
            leo("And something to try today?"),
