    private val de8Words = Podcast(
        "de8-words",
        listOf(
            maya("Hi, and welcome back. Today is the body, feeling ill and the doctor. By the end you can tell a doctor what hurts, in two different ways, and ask for the right piece of paper."),
            jonas("Mein Kopf tut weh. [repeat]", "My head hurts."),
            leo("Straight in with a headache. [chuckle] What's going on in that sentence?"),
            maya("It works like English: my head hurts. «der Kopf» is the head, and «tut weh» means hurts. The head is the one doing the hurting. Now let's collect body parts, each with its article. Picture yourself pointing at your face, from the top down."),
            jonas("der Kopf, das Auge, das Ohr, die Nase, der Mund. [repeat]", "the head, the eye, the ear, the nose, the mouth."),
            leo("Three different articles in five words. How do I keep them straight?"),
            maya("Learn each word with its article, like a name tag. Most of the body is «der»: «der Hals», the throat, «der Bauch», the stomach, «der Rücken», the back, «der Fuß», the foot. Watch the «das» ones: «das Auge», «das Ohr», «das Bein», the leg, and «das Herz», the heart. And «die Nase» and «die Hand»."),
            jonas("der Hals, der Bauch, der Rücken, das Bein, der Fuß. [repeat]", "the throat, the stomach, the back, the leg, the foot."),
            leo("Okay. And the second way to say something hurts?"),
            maya("The second way builds one long word. Take the body part and glue «Schmerzen», pain, on the end. Head plus pain is «Kopfschmerzen». And you say you have it."),
            jonas("Ich habe Kopfschmerzen. [repeat]", "I have a headache."),
            leo("Why not «ich bin»? In English I'd say I am in pain."),
            maya("Because «Schmerzen» is a noun, a thing you have, so it always takes «haben», never «sein». And the body part comes first: «Bauchschmerzen» is stomach ache, «Zahnschmerzen» is toothache. Picture Usaid at breakfast, holding his jaw."),
            jonas("Ich habe Zahnschmerzen. Mein Bauch tut auch weh. [repeat]", "I have toothache. My stomach hurts too."),
            leo("Poor Usaid. And if he has a cold?"),
            maya("Then he names the illness, with «haben» again. A cold is «die Erkältung», a fever is «das Fieber», a cough is «der Husten», and the flu is «die Grippe»."),
            jonas("Ich habe eine Erkältung und Fieber. [repeat]", "I have a cold and a fever."),
            leo("And if I've had it for a while? The doctor wants to know that, right?"),
            maya("Yes, and German uses «seit», since or for, with the present tense. English says I have had a fever for two days. German says, I have a fever since two days."),
            jonas("Ich habe seit zwei Tagen Fieber. [repeat]", "I have had a fever for two days."),
            leo("And if I just feel rotten in general, nothing in particular?"),
            maya("Then use the pattern from how are you: it goes badly for me. But at the pharmacy, don't stop there. They need the symptom, not just the verdict, so add what hurts."),
            jonas("Mir geht es schlecht. Ich habe Halsschmerzen. [repeat]", "I feel unwell. I have a sore throat."),
            leo("Now the admin. Where do I actually go?"),
            maya("Your doctor's surgery is «die Praxis», and it has «Sprechstunde», surgery hours. For a tooth you go to «der Zahnarzt», the dentist. The hospital is «das Krankenhaus». And at the surgery they always ask about your health insurance, «die Krankenkasse»."),
            leo("And the piece of paper you promised?"),
            maya("Two papers, and people mix them up. «das Rezept» is the prescription. You take it to «die Apotheke», the pharmacy. Funny thing: «Rezept» also means a cooking recipe. And «die Krankmeldung» is the sick note for work or school."),
            jonas("Ich brauche eine Krankmeldung für die Arbeit. [repeat]", "I need a sick note for work."),
            leo("And at the pharmacy, what do I get?"),
            maya("You hand over the «Rezept», and you get «das Medikament», the medicine, often «Tabletten», tablets. The pharmacist tells you how many."),
            jonas("Hier ist das Rezept. Zwei Tabletten am Tag. [repeat]", "Here is the prescription. Two tablets a day."),
            leo("And what do I say to Sanya when she's ill?"),
            maya("The kind wish: get well soon. Literally, good betterment. You say it as you leave, or at the end of a message."),
            jonas("Gute Besserung, Sanya! [repeat]", "Get well soon, Sanya!"),
            leo("So what should I remember for the Goethe exam?"),
            maya("Three things. In the listening part, catch the body part in front of «schmerzen»: «Kopf», «Bauch» or «Zahn» is the whole answer. In the speaking part, say what hurts both ways: «Mein Hals tut weh», or «Ich habe Halsschmerzen». And keep the papers apart: «Rezept» for the pharmacy, «Krankmeldung» for work."),
            leo("And something to try today?"),
            maya("Pick three different body parts and say what hurts, both ways. «Ich habe», then the body part with «schmerzen», for each. Then «Mein», the body part, and «tut weh», for each. Say one symptom with «seit», like «seit zwei Tagen». Then name what you would ask the doctor for: a «Rezept», or a «Krankmeldung»."),
            jonas("Bleib gesund! Tschüss!", "Stay healthy! Bye!"),
            leo("Stay healthy, everyone. See you next time."),
        ),
        series = PodcastSeries.GERMAN_A1,
    )

    private val de8Grammar = Podcast(
        "de8-grammar",
        listOf(
            maya("Welcome back. Today is the «Imperativ», the command form: how a doctor, a sign or a friend tells you what to do. And one small pattern you already know from how are you."),
