            leo("That sounds like a question. Drink you a lot of water?"),
            maya("[chuckle] That's the trick. The polite «Sie» command is the yes or no question turned into an instruction. Verb first, «Sie» second, and a full stop instead of a question mark. Picture the doctor in «die Praxis», in a white coat. A stranger, so «Sie»."),
            jonas("Nehmen Sie die Tabletten! Bleiben Sie im Bett! [repeat]", "Take the tablets! Stay in bed!"),
            leo("Can I drop the «Sie»? It's shorter."),
            maya("No, «Sie» stays. Without it, it's not polite any more, or not German at all. And «bitte» makes any command softer. Say Frau Weber knocks on your office door, and you invite her to sit down."),
            jonas("Kommen Sie herein! Nehmen Sie bitte Platz. [repeat]", "Come in! Please take a seat."),
            leo("And «herein»?"),
            maya("In, inside. Now the friendly command, for one friend, with «du». Here's the picture: take the «du» form of the verb and cut off the «st» at the end. «du trinkst» becomes «trink»."),
            jonas("Trink viel! Bleib im Bett! [repeat]", "Drink a lot! Stay in bed!"),
