            jonas("Rufen Sie morgen in der Praxis an! [repeat]", "Call the surgery tomorrow!"),
            leo("Okay, commands done. You said there was a pattern from how are you?"),
            maya("Yes. «Mir geht es gut» uses «mir», not «ich». It's a «Dativpronomen», the to-me form: literally, it goes well to me. You only need a few: «mir», «dir», «ihm», «ihr», «Ihnen» and «uns»."),
            jonas("Wie geht es dir? Mir geht es nicht gut. [repeat]", "How are you? I'm not well."),
            leo("So «Ich geht es gut» is wrong?"),
            maya("Wrong, and very common. Always «mir». For someone you call «Sie», it's «Ihnen», with a capital. The doctor uses it to ask what's wrong with you, and a shop assistant uses it to offer help."),
            jonas("Was fehlt Ihnen? Kann ich Ihnen helfen? [repeat]", "What's wrong? Can I help you?"),
            leo("And for him or her?"),
            maya("«ihm» for him, «ihr» for her. Say Usaid's back hurts, and you ask if Sanya is better."),
